## Required work before a timing freeze

1. Decide and preregister validation placement. Full arena validation is appropriate for correctness but would add a redundant traversal inside a performance endpoint. The recommended timed path is `validate=False` with the O(1) ownership check, while full validation runs immediately outside every timed block.
2. Complete and freeze host, interpreter, affinity/power, GC, session/block, batch, timeout, memory, storage, and wall-budget fields.
3. Fix new synthetic/bootstrap seeds and freeze the fresh natural acquisition/admission process. Do not inspect or generate those holdouts before the freeze.
4. Hash a dedicated timing harness and analysis implementation. The correctness runner must not be repurposed as a timer.
5. Review and sign the final preregistration and freeze record, then request separate authorization for holdout generation and timing.

Until those items are complete, do not run performance pilots on P15 as confirmatory evidence, generate a fresh holdout, modify production, commit, push, or deploy.
